{"content_text": "{\"protocolSection\":{\"identificationModule\":{\"nctId\":\"NCT06578949\",\"orgStudyIdInfo\":{\"id\":\"D9289C00008\"},\"secondaryIdInfos\":[{\"id\":\"ALXN1210-PNH-323\",\"type\":\"OTHER\",\"domain\":\"Alexion\"}],\"organization\":{\"fullName\":\"Alexion Pharmaceuticals, Inc.\",\"class\":\"INDUSTRY\"},\"briefTitle\":\"Efficacy, Safety, Pharmacokinetics, Pharmacodynamics, and Immunogenicity of Ravulizumab in Chinese Adults Participants With Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria (PNH)\",\"officialTitle\":\"A Phase 3, Single-arm, Open-label, Multicenter Study to Assess the Efficacy, Safety, Pharmacokinetics, Pharmacodynamics, and Immunogenicity of Ravulizumab in Complement Inhibitor Treatment Naïve Adult Participants With Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria (PNH) in China\"},\"statusModule\":{\"statusVerifiedDate\":\"2026-05\",\"overallStatus\":\"COMPLETED\",\"expandedAccessInfo\":{\"hasExpandedAccess\":false},\"startDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2024-10-10\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"primaryCompletionDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2025-05-15\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"completionDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2025-12-22\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"studyFirstSubmitDate\":\"2024-08-28\",\"studyFirstSubmitQcDate\":\"2024-08-28\",\"studyFirstPostDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2024-08-30\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"resultsFirstSubmitDate\":\"2026-05-11\",\"resultsFirstSubmitQcDate\":\"2026-05-11\",\"resultsFirstPostDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2026-06-05\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"},\"lastUpdateSubmitDate\":\"2026-05-11\",\"lastUpdatePostDateStruct\":{\"date\":\"2026-06-05\",\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"}},\"sponsorCollaboratorsModule\":{\"responsibleParty\":{\"type\":\"SPONSOR\"},\"leadSponsor\":{\"name\":\"Alexion Pharmaceuticals, Inc.\",\"class\":\"INDUSTRY\"}},\"oversightModule\":{\"oversightHasDmc\":false,\"isFdaRegulatedDrug\":true,\"isFdaRegulatedDevice\":false},\"descriptionModule\":{\"briefSummary\":\"The primary objective of this study is to evaluate the efficacy of ravulizumab in adult participants with PNH.\"},\"conditionsModule\":{\"conditions\":[\"Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria\",\"PNH\"],\"keywords\":[\"Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria\",\"PNH\",\"Ravulizumab\"]},\"designModule\":{\"studyType\":\"INTERVENTIONAL\",\"phases\":[\"PHASE3\"],\"designInfo\":{\"allocation\":\"NA\",\"interventionModel\":\"SINGLE_GROUP\",\"primaryPurpose\":\"TREATMENT\",\"maskingInfo\":{\"masking\":\"NONE\"}},\"enrollmentInfo\":{\"count\":18,\"type\":\"ACTUAL\"}},\"armsInterventionsModule\":{\"armGroups\":[{\"label\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"type\":\"EXPERIMENTAL\",\"description\":\"During the Primary Treatment Period, participants will receive a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks. On Day 183, all participants will enter a 32-week Extension Treatment Period and receive ravulizumab. Beginning on Day 183, participants will receive a maintenance dose of ravulizumab q8w for an additional 32 weeks.\",\"interventionNames\":[\"Drug: Ravulizumab\"]}],\"interventions\":[{\"type\":\"DRUG\",\"name\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Ravulizumab will be administered by intravenous (IV) infusion.\",\"armGroupLabels\":[\"Ravulizumab\"],\"otherNames\":[\"ALXN1210\"]}]},\"outcomesModule\":{\"primaryOutcomes\":[{\"measure\":\"Percentage Change in Lactate Dehydrogenase (LDH) From Baseline to Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"LDH is an indicator of intravascular hemolysis that occurs in participants with paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria. A decrease in LDH indicated reduction (improvement) in hemolysis. Baseline was defined as the average of all available on-study assessments prior to the first dose of study drug. The percent change in LDH was analyzed using a mixed-effect model for repeated measures (MMRM) with the fixed categorical effect of visit, fixed continuous effect of the LDH baseline value as covariates, and participant as random effect.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 183 (Week 26)\"}],\"secondaryOutcomes\":[{\"measure\":\"Percentage of Participants Achieving LDH <1.5 * Upper Limit of Normal (ULN) at Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"LDH is an indicator of intravascular hemolysis that occurs in participants with paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria. A decrease in LDH indicated reduction (improvement) in hemolysis. Baseline was defined as the average of all available on-study assessments prior to the first dose of study drug.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 183 (Week 26)\"},{\"measure\":\"Percentage of Participants Achieving Transfusion Avoidance Through Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"Transfusion avoidance was defined as the percentage of participants who remained transfusion free and did not require a transfusion per protocol-specified guidelines (hemoglobin value of ≤9 grams (g)/deciliter (dL) with signs or symptoms of sufficient severity to warrant a transfusion, or a hemoglobin value of ≤7 g/dL regardless of presence of clinical signs or symptoms) through Day 183.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 183 (Week 26)\"},{\"measure\":\"Percentage of Participants Experiencing Breakthrough Hemolysis Through Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"Breakthrough hemolysis was defined as at least one new or worsening symptom or sign of intravascular hemolysis (fatigue, hemoglobinuria, abdominal pain, dyspnea, anemia \\\\[hemoglobin \\\\<10 g/dL\\\\], major adverse vascular event \\\\[including thrombosis\\\\], dysphagia, or erectile dysfunction) in the presence of elevated LDH ≥2 times the ULN.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 183 (Week 26)\"},{\"measure\":\"Change in Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy-Fatigue Scale (FACIT-Fatigue) Score From Baseline to Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"The FACIT-Fatigue is a 13-item questionnaire that assesses self-reported fatigue and its impact upon daily activities and function over the preceding 7 days. Participants scored each item on a 5-point scale: 0 (Not at all) to 4 (Very much). Total scores range from 0 to 52, with a higher score indicating better quality of life. Analysis was using a mixed-effect model for repeated measures (MMRM) with the fixed categorical effect of visit, fixed continuous effect of the baseline value of FACIT-Fatigue score as covariates, and participant as random effect.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 183 (Week 26)\"},{\"measure\":\"Change in Hemoglobin (Hgb) From Baseline to Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"Analysis was performed using MMRM with the fixed categorical effect of visit, fixed continuous effect of the Hgb baseline value as covariates, and participant as random effect.\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 183 (Week 26)\"}]},\"eligibilityModule\":{\"eligibilityCriteria\":\"Inclusion Criteria:\\n\\n* Adult C5 inhibitor naive PNH patients (age\\\\>=18), which is confirmed by flow cytometry evaluation.\\n* Must be vaccinated againast N meningitidis.\\n\\nExclusion Criteria\\n\\n* Meningitidis infection or unresolved meningococcal disease\\n* History of bone marrow transplantation\\n* Other significant systemic diseases that might have impact on efficacy and safety assessment\",\"healthyVolunteers\":false,\"sex\":\"ALL\",\"minimumAge\":\"18 Years\",\"stdAges\":[\"ADULT\",\"OLDER_ADULT\"]},\"contactsLocationsModule\":{\"locations\":[{\"facility\":\"Research Site\",\"city\":\"Beijing\",\"zip\":\"CN-100730\",\"country\":\"China\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":39.9075,\"lon\":116.39723}},{\"facility\":\"Research Site\",\"city\":\"Guangzhou\",\"zip\":\"510100\",\"country\":\"China\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":23.11667,\"lon\":113.25}},{\"facility\":\"Research Site\",\"city\":\"Hangzhou\",\"zip\":\"310003\",\"country\":\"China\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":30.29365,\"lon\":120.16142}},{\"facility\":\"Research Site\",\"city\":\"Nantong\",\"zip\":\"226001\",\"country\":\"China\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":32.03028,\"lon\":120.87472}},{\"facility\":\"Research Site\",\"city\":\"Shanghai\",\"zip\":\"200040\",\"country\":\"China\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":31.22222,\"lon\":121.45806}},{\"facility\":\"Research Site\",\"city\":\"Tianjin\",\"zip\":\"300020\",\"country\":\"China\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":39.14222,\"lon\":117.17667}},{\"facility\":\"Research Site\",\"city\":\"Tianjin\",\"zip\":\"300050\",\"country\":\"China\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":39.14222,\"lon\":117.17667}},{\"facility\":\"Research Site\",\"city\":\"Wuhan\",\"zip\":\"430022\",\"country\":\"China\",\"geoPoint\":{\"lat\":30.58333,\"lon\":114.26667}}]},\"referencesModule\":{\"seeAlsoLinks\":[{\"label\":\"Related Info\",\"url\":\"https://filehosting-v2.pharmacm.com/api/Attachment/Download?tenantId=80217111&amp;parentIdentifier=D9289C00008&amp;attachmentIdentifier=1fba3773-7ccf-47fa-8600-8a06c7f4ac75&amp;fileName=ALXN1210-PNH-323_d9289c00008-study-synopsis-en_Redacted.pdf&amp;versionIdentifier=\"}]},\"ipdSharingStatementModule\":{\"ipdSharing\":\"YES\",\"description\":\"Alexion has a public commitment to allow requests for access to study data and will be supplying a protocol, CSR, and plain language summaries.\",\"infoTypes\":[\"STUDY_PROTOCOL\",\"SAP\",\"CSR\"]}},\"resultsSection\":{\"participantFlowModule\":{\"preAssignmentDetails\":\"The study included a 26-week Primary Treatment Period, and an additional 32-week Extension Treatment Period. The results for the Primary Treatment Period have been reported. Final analysis data will be reported after completion of the 32-week Extension Treatment Period.\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"FG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\"}],\"periods\":[{\"title\":\"Overall Study\",\"milestones\":[{\"type\":\"STARTED\",\"achievements\":[{\"groupId\":\"FG000\",\"numSubjects\":\"18\"}]},{\"type\":\"Received at Least 1 Dose of Study Drug\",\"achievements\":[{\"groupId\":\"FG000\",\"numSubjects\":\"18\"}]},{\"type\":\"COMPLETED\",\"comment\":\"Completed Primary Treatment Period\",\"achievements\":[{\"groupId\":\"FG000\",\"numSubjects\":\"18\"}]},{\"type\":\"NOT COMPLETED\",\"achievements\":[{\"groupId\":\"FG000\",\"numSubjects\":\"0\"}]}]}]},\"baselineCharacteristicsModule\":{\"populationDescription\":\"Full Analysis Set (FAS) included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose (full or partial) of the study intervention.\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"BG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"18\"}]}],\"measures\":[{\"title\":\"Age, Continuous\",\"paramType\":\"MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"STANDARD_DEVIATION\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"years\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"42.8\",\"spread\":\"10.4\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Sex: Female, Male\",\"paramType\":\"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Participants\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"title\":\"Female\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"3\"}]},{\"title\":\"Male\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"15\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Ethnicity (NIH/OMB)\",\"paramType\":\"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Participants\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"title\":\"Hispanic or Latino\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Not Hispanic or Latino\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"18\"}]},{\"title\":\"Unknown or Not Reported\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]}]},{\"title\":\"Race (NIH/OMB)\",\"paramType\":\"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"Participants\",\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"title\":\"American Indian or Alaska Native\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Asian\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"18\"}]},{\"title\":\"Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Black or African American\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"White\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"More than one race\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]},{\"title\":\"Unknown or Not Reported\",\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"BG000\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]}]}]},\"outcomeMeasuresModule\":{\"outcomeMeasures\":[{\"type\":\"PRIMARY\",\"title\":\"Percentage Change in Lactate Dehydrogenase (LDH) From Baseline to Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"LDH is an indicator of intravascular hemolysis that occurs in participants with paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria. A decrease in LDH indicated reduction (improvement) in hemolysis. Baseline was defined as the average of all available on-study assessments prior to the first dose of study drug. The percent change in LDH was analyzed using a mixed-effect model for repeated measures (MMRM) with the fixed categorical effect of visit, fixed continuous effect of the LDH baseline value as covariates, and participant as random effect.\",\"populationDescription\":\"FAS included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose (full or partial) of the study intervention. 'Overall number of participants analyzed' = participants evaluable for this outcome measure.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"LEAST_SQUARES_MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"95% Confidence Interval\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"percent change\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"17\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"-81.3\",\"lowerLimit\":\"-84.2\",\"upperLimit\":\"-78.3\"}]}]}],\"analyses\":[{\"groupIds\":[\"OG000\"],\"nonInferiorityType\":\"OTHER\",\"pValue\":\"< 0.001\",\"statisticalMethod\":\"Mixed Models Analysis\"}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Percentage of Participants Achieving LDH <1.5 * Upper Limit of Normal (ULN) at Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"LDH is an indicator of intravascular hemolysis that occurs in participants with paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria. A decrease in LDH indicated reduction (improvement) in hemolysis. Baseline was defined as the average of all available on-study assessments prior to the first dose of study drug.\",\"populationDescription\":\"FAS included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose (full or partial) of the study intervention. 'Overall number of participants analyzed' = participants evaluable for this outcome measure.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"dispersionType\":\"95% Confidence Interval\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"percentage of participants\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"17\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"94.1\",\"lowerLimit\":\"71.3\",\"upperLimit\":\"99.9\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Percentage of Participants Achieving Transfusion Avoidance Through Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"Transfusion avoidance was defined as the percentage of participants who remained transfusion free and did not require a transfusion per protocol-specified guidelines (hemoglobin value of ≤9 grams (g)/deciliter (dL) with signs or symptoms of sufficient severity to warrant a transfusion, or a hemoglobin value of ≤7 g/dL regardless of presence of clinical signs or symptoms) through Day 183.\",\"populationDescription\":\"FAS included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose (full or partial) of the study intervention.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"dispersionType\":\"95% Confidence Interval\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"percentage of participants\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"18\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"94.4\",\"lowerLimit\":\"72.7\",\"upperLimit\":\"99.9\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Percentage of Participants Experiencing Breakthrough Hemolysis Through Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"Breakthrough hemolysis was defined as at least one new or worsening symptom or sign of intravascular hemolysis (fatigue, hemoglobinuria, abdominal pain, dyspnea, anemia \\\\[hemoglobin \\\\<10 g/dL\\\\], major adverse vascular event \\\\[including thrombosis\\\\], dysphagia, or erectile dysfunction) in the presence of elevated LDH ≥2 times the ULN.\",\"populationDescription\":\"FAS included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose (full or partial) of the study intervention.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"NUMBER\",\"dispersionType\":\"95% Confidence Interval\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"percentage of participants\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"18\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\",\"lowerLimit\":\"0.0\",\"upperLimit\":\"18.5\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change in Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy-Fatigue Scale (FACIT-Fatigue) Score From Baseline to Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"The FACIT-Fatigue is a 13-item questionnaire that assesses self-reported fatigue and its impact upon daily activities and function over the preceding 7 days. Participants scored each item on a 5-point scale: 0 (Not at all) to 4 (Very much). Total scores range from 0 to 52, with a higher score indicating better quality of life. Analysis was using a mixed-effect model for repeated measures (MMRM) with the fixed categorical effect of visit, fixed continuous effect of the baseline value of FACIT-Fatigue score as covariates, and participant as random effect.\",\"populationDescription\":\"FAS included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose (full or partial) of the study intervention.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"LEAST_SQUARES_MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"95% Confidence Interval\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"units on a scale\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"18\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"4.5\",\"lowerLimit\":\"1.3\",\"upperLimit\":\"7.7\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change in Hemoglobin (Hgb) From Baseline to Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"description\":\"Analysis was performed using MMRM with the fixed categorical effect of visit, fixed continuous effect of the Hgb baseline value as covariates, and participant as random effect.\",\"populationDescription\":\"FAS included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose (full or partial) of the study intervention.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"paramType\":\"LEAST_SQUARES_MEAN\",\"dispersionType\":\"95% Confidence Interval\",\"unitOfMeasure\":\"g/liter (L)\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline, Day 183 (Week 26)\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"18\"}]}],\"classes\":[{\"categories\":[{\"measurements\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"26.6\",\"lowerLimit\":\"13.8\",\"upperLimit\":\"39.3\"}]}]}]}]},\"adverseEventsModule\":{\"frequencyThreshold\":\"0\",\"timeFrame\":\"Baseline up to Week 26\",\"description\":\"Safety Set included all enrolled participants who received at least 1 dose (full or partial) of the study intervention.\",\"eventGroups\":[{\"id\":\"EG000\",\"title\":\"Ravulizumab\",\"description\":\"Participants received a weight-based loading dose of ravulizumab on Day 1 followed by weight-based maintenance dose of ravulizumab on Day 15 and once every 8 weeks (q8w) thereafter for a total of 26 weeks in Primary Treatment Period.\",\"deathsNumAffected\":0,\"deathsNumAtRisk\":18,\"seriousNumAffected\":2,\"seriousNumAtRisk\":18,\"otherNumAffected\":16,\"otherNumAtRisk\":18}],\"seriousEvents\":[{\"term\":\"Liver injury\",\"organSystem\":\"Hepatobiliary disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA 28.0\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":18}]},{\"term\":\"Pyrexia\",\"organSystem\":\"General disorders\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA 28.0\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":18}]}],\"otherEvents\":[{\"term\":\"Influenza\",\"organSystem\":\"Infections and infestations\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA 28.0\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":18}]},{\"term\":\"Periodontitis\",\"organSystem\":\"Infections and infestations\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA 28.0\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":18}]},{\"term\":\"Sinusitis\",\"organSystem\":\"Infections and infestations\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA 28.0\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":18}]},{\"term\":\"Tinea pedis\",\"organSystem\":\"Infections and infestations\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA 28.0\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numAffected\":1,\"numAtRisk\":18}]},{\"term\":\"Upper respiratory tract infection\",\"organSystem\":\"Infections and infestations\",\"sourceVocabulary\":\"MedDRA 28.0\",\"assessmentType\":\"SYSTEMATIC_ASSESSMENT\",\"stats\":[{\"groupId\":\"EG000\",\"numAffected\":4,\"numAtRisk\":18}]},{\"term\":\"Decreased appetite\",\"organSystem\":\"Metaboli